From: Bouteillepleine <76688492+Bouteillepleine@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: tcp: bbr3: own the private ctx per socket (5.10-6.6)

Same defect and same fix as the 6.12 patch, cut against the four older
backports. They share one shape: no bbr3_ctx_if_active(), a bbr3_release()
that frees straight out of slot 0, and a tcp_notify_skb_loss_event() that
reads the slot inline.

sk_clone_lock() byte-copies the whole inet_connection_sock, so a passive-open
child inherits both icsk_ca_priv slot 0 -- the struct bbr3 * -- and
icsk_ca_initialized from its parent, and inet_csk_clone_lock() clears neither.
If the parent's congestion control was already initialized before the clone,
tcp_init_transfer() skips tcp_init_congestion_control() for the child because
icsk_ca_initialized is already 1. bbr3_init() therefore never runs for that
child and it uses the parent's heap ctx for its whole lifetime, and
tcp_cleanup_congestion_control() calls .release unconditionally, so every such
child frees the parent's still-live ctx: a double kmem_cache_free plus a
use-after-free in the parent, with concurrent children mutating one shared BBR
state in between.

Upstream BBR cannot hit this because its state lives inline in icsk_ca_priv,
where the byte copy hands the child an independent copy. Storing a pointer
there instead -- which is what keeps struct tcp_sock and struct rate_sample
byte-identical for KMI -- is what turns that copy into shared ownership.

No reachable trigger is known on a stock stack. A listener is the only clone
source TCP has, and neither path that could initialize one does so:
tcp_assign_congestion_control() never calls .init, and
tcp_reinit_congestion_control(), where setsockopt(TCP_CONGESTION) lands, skips
it outright --

	if (!((1 << sk->sk_state) & (TCPF_CLOSE | TCPF_LISTEN)))
		tcp_init_congestion_control(sk);

-- so a listener reaches accept() with icsk_ca_initialized still 0 and slot 0
still NULL, and tcp_init_transfer() then runs init for every child, which
allocates each one its own ctx. This patch is therefore hardening of the
ownership invariant, not a fix for an observed corruption. The only documented
way the flag arrives already set is the case tcp_init_transfer() names in its
own comment, BPF initializing congestion control ahead of it.

Record the owning socket in the ctx and test it in bbr3_get_priv(), the single
accessor every BBR callback goes through, so a ctx the socket does not own
reads as absent and the guarded callbacks take the existing fail-closed Reno
dispatch rather than another socket's state. bbr3_release() then frees only
what bbr3_init() allocated for that same socket, and the inline slot read in
tcp_notify_skb_loss_event() gets the same test. struct bbr3 sits behind the
opaque icsk_ca_priv u64[], so the added member carries no CRC impact.

One patch covers android12-5.10, android13-5.15, android14-6.1 and
android15-6.6: all five pre-images occur exactly once and byte-identical in
each of the four.
---
--- a/include/net/tcp.h
+++ b/include/net/tcp.h
@@ -2343,6 +2343,8 @@
 
 	/* react to a specific lost skb (optional) */
 	void (*skb_marked_lost)(struct sock *sk, const struct sk_buff *skb);
+
+	const struct sock *owner;
 };
 
 /* At how many usecs into the future should the RTO fire? */
--- a/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr3.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr3.c
@@ -288,7 +288,9 @@
 static inline struct bbr3 *bbr3_get_priv(const struct sock *sk)
 {
 	/* Read the address value out of slot 0 of the 104-byte array space */
-	return *(struct bbr3 **)inet_csk_ca(sk);
+	struct bbr3 *bbr = *(struct bbr3 **)inet_csk_ca(sk);
+
+	return (bbr && bbr->owner == sk) ? bbr : NULL;
 }
 
 /* This connection can use ECN if both endpoints have signaled ECN support in
@@ -2038,6 +2040,7 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	bbr->owner = sk;
 	*bbr3_ptr = bbr;
 
 	WRITE_ONCE(bbr->skb_marked_lost, bbr3_skb_marked_lost);
@@ -2125,13 +2128,13 @@
 __used noinline static void bbr3_release(struct sock *sk)
 {
 	struct bbr3 **bbr3_ptr = (struct bbr3 **)inet_csk_ca(sk);
+	struct bbr3 *bbr = *bbr3_ptr;
 
 	tcp_sk(sk)->ecn_flags &= ~TCP_ECN_ECT_PERMANENT;
+	*bbr3_ptr = NULL;
 
-	if (*bbr3_ptr) {
-		kmem_cache_free(bbr3_cache, *bbr3_ptr);
-		*bbr3_ptr = NULL;
-	}
+	if (bbr && bbr->owner == sk)
+		kmem_cache_free(bbr3_cache, bbr);
 }
 
 /* BBR marks the current round trip as a loss round. */
--- a/net/ipv4/tcp_input.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/tcp_input.c
@@ -1093,6 +1093,8 @@
 		void (*hook)(struct sock *, const struct sk_buff *);
 
 		bbr3 = *(struct bbr3 **)inet_csk_ca(sk);
+		if (bbr3 && bbr3->owner != sk)
+			bbr3 = NULL;
 		hook = bbr3 ? READ_ONCE(bbr3->skb_marked_lost) : NULL;
 		if (hook)
 			hook(sk, skb);
